Snowflake Views — Summary

Snowflake supports multiple types of views:

Standard Views
Materialized Views
Secure Views
Secure Materialized Views
1. Standard View

A standard view:

Stores only the SQL query definition
Does NOT store data physically

Example:

CREATE VIEW vw_sales AS
SELECT customer_id, amount
FROM sales;

When users query the view:

Snowflake reads data from the underlying table.
Key Points
Advantages
No storage cost
Simplifies complex queries
Restricts rows/columns
Reusable logic
Limitations
Performance depends on source query
Data retrieved from base table each time
Important Exam Point

If source table is dropped:

View becomes invalid
Queries fail with object does not exist error
2. Materialized View

A Materialized View:

Stores query results physically
Precomputed dataset
Automatically refreshed

Example:

CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW mv_sales AS
SELECT customer_id, SUM(amount)
FROM sales
GROUP BY customer_id;
Key Points
Advantages
Faster query performance
Precomputed results
Useful for expensive aggregations
Limitations
Storage cost exists
Background maintenance cost exists
Important Interview Point

Snowflake automatically refreshes materialized views.

Snowflake manages compute automatically.

That makes Materialized Views:

A serverless feature
3. Secure Views

A Secure View:

Hides query definition from unauthorized users

Example:

CREATE SECURE VIEW secure_sales AS
SELECT * FROM sales;
Why Use Secure Views?

Used for:

Sensitive data
PII protection
Data sharing
Regulatory compliance
Important Security Behavior

Without SECURE:

Users may see view definition using:
GET_DDL
DESCRIBE VIEW
SHOW VIEWS

With SECURE:

Unauthorized users cannot see the definition.
4. Performance Impact of Secure Views

Important interview/certification point:

Secure views may perform slower.

Reason:

Some optimizer optimizations are disabled
to avoid accidental data exposure.
5. Standard View vs Materialized View
Standard View	Materialized View
Stores query only	Stores data physically
No storage cost	Storage cost
Query runs every time	Precomputed results
Slower for heavy aggregations	Faster
No refresh maintenance	Auto-maintained
6. Secure View vs Standard View
Standard View	Secure View
Query definition visible	Hidden from unauthorized users
Better performance	Slightly slower sometimes
Normal optimizer behavior	Restricted optimizations
