Strong Final Interview Answer

Snowflake supports Standard Views, Materialized Views, and Secure Views. Standard views store only query definitions and do not physically store data, making them cost efficient but dependent on runtime query execution. Materialized views physically store precomputed query results and are automatically refreshed by Snowflake, improving query performance for heavy aggregations and repeated queries. Secure views protect sensitive query logic by hiding definitions from unauthorized users, though they may have slightly lower performance because certain optimizer optimizations are disabled for security reasons.
